    "description": "Developer\n• Developer on the VCS21 project, a cannot-fail net-centric air traffic controller VOIP based communication infrastructure.\n• Implemented and integrated two features into code base.\n▪ Interfaced with hardware status indicators that visually indicated instantaneous state of the embedded device.\n▪ Developed and integrated a new communication configuration into front and back-end software after examining software\nspecification documents, evaluating code base against requirements, and determining that code base did not meet specifications.\n• Repaired and maintained mission critical code to ensure hardening and resiliency against catastrophic failure. Repaired root cause of hard\ncrashes that paralyzed the system.\n• Built and maintained amicable relationships with peers locally and overseas.\nLaboratory management\n• Installed, maintained, and provided network administration for VCS21 embedded devices and supporting hardware.\n• Ensured that applications installed on VCS21 embedded devices were up-to-date.\nReverse Engineering\n• Reverse engineered VCS21 software from source code to write Software Description Documents (SwDD), Feature Description Documents\n(FDD), and Interface Control Documents (ICD) for the FAA and National Air Traffic Services (United Kingdom).\n• Created 100’s of UML compliant diagrams and mapped 1000’s of requirements to them.",
